{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "FastJX",
    "description": "Fast-JX photolysis rates, upstream `FastJX_interpolation_troposphere(t_ref; mech = :superfast)`: no radiation is computed at run time - the 18 band actinic fluxes are bilinear (P, cosSZA) lookups of upstream's offline precompute of the online FastJX (direct beam + clear-sky diffuse field at each node), scaled by the Earth-Sun distance factor. 0-D and stateless; same inputs, cross sections and 13 J-rates as fastjx.esm.",
    "authors": ["GasChem.jl / GasChemMTK.jl contributors", "EarthSciModels"],
    "created": "2026-10-28T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": ["chemistry", "photolysis", "fast-jx", "interp-linear", "interp-bilinear"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Wild, O., Zhu, X., and Prather, M. J. (2000), Fast-J: Accurate simulation of in- and below-cloud photolysis in tropospheric chemical models, J. Atmos. Chem., 37, 245-282."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Neu, J. L., Prather, M. J., and Penner, J. E. (2007), Global atmospheric chemistry: Integrating over fractional cloud cover, J. Geophys. Res., 112, D11306, doi:10.1029/2006JD008007."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Cross sections and quantum yields on the 18-bin grid of GEOS-Chem's CHEM_INPUTS/CLOUD_J/v2024-09 FJX_spec.dat (bins 17-18 at 380/574 nm); clear-sky diffuse field from a Julia port of the Cloud-J Feautrier solver (geoschem/cloud-j@16d18b07)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: jialinl6/GasChemMTK.jl@37792b29 (branch superfast-gas-only), src/Fast-JX.jl, src/direct_flux.jl, src/interpolations_FastJX.jl, src/tropospheric_interpolation_data.bson, src/diffuse_flux_data.bson."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "FastJX": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: jialinl6/GasChemMTK.jl@37792b29 (branch superfast-gas-only):src/interpolations_FastJX.jl FastJX_interpolation_troposphere (mech = :superfast).\n\nFlux table: tropospheric_interpolation_data.bson as regenerated upstream by scripts/scattering/precompute_table.jl (23 P nodes 1000-100000 Pa x 61 cosSZA nodes -0.2..1.0, total = calc_direct_flux + Cloud-J diffuse at each node, solf applied at run time). It agrees with the online fastjx.esm exactly at the nodes. Between them the two differ by what interpolation does to the direct beam, which the online model holds piecewise constant on the 73 GEOS edges: against upstream's online FastJX the six SuperFast J's here are within 0.43% at the surface over a full day while cosSZA >= 0.05 (2.2% in twilight), within 0.7% at 950 hPa, and up to 9.6% at 300 hPa at low sun (cosSZA ~0.05).\n\nInterface change: cosSZA is computed internally from (t + t_ref, lat, long) as upstream does. The previous revision took cos_sza as an input parameter; a host that set it now sets lat/long/t_ref instead.\n\nWhat is transcribed verbatim from upstream: cos_solar_zenith_angle (its own declination/equation-of-time formula, NOT lib/solar.esm's NOAA Spencer series, including upstream's abs(lat) - southern-hemisphere points get the northern-hemisphere seasonal declination term - and its mod(year, 4) leap rule); solar_flux_factor; every cross section and quantum yield the 13 rates use, knot for knot as the reference evaluates them (bins whose two temperature rows agree within Float32 isapprox are the constant upstream returns); ActAld's cross section on the pressure axis (P/100, hPa) as upstream's _FJX_PRESSURE_AXIS_J requires; adjust_j_o31D. The J set is upstream's `mech = :superfast` list (the rates SuperFast and Pollu consume); upstream FastJX also exposes ~95 GEOS-Chem channels that are not carried here. datetime.* decomposes t_utc with integer seconds, where Julia's unix2datetime rounds to the millisecond; the two differ only within 0.5 ms of a second boundary.\n\nTolerance rationale (rel = 1e-06): expected values are the reference package's own functions at the test inputs; the ESM repeats the same Float64 arithmetic on the same tables, leaving roundoff (and upstream's Float32 cross-section slope); measured, the worst assertion here is off by 3.0e-8 relative, and the worst over 17 outputs at 300 random (t, lat, long, T, P, H2O) points is 3.3e-8. abs = 1e-22 floors rates that are exactly 0 at night."
      },
      "variables": {
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 298.0,
          "description": "Air temperature (K). Selects the temperature-dependent cross sections and O(1D) quantum yields and enters adjust_j_o31D. Upstream default 298 K."
        },
        "P": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "Pa",
          "default": 101325.0,
          "description": "Air pressure (Pa). Selects the actinic-flux level and enters adjust_j_o31D; ActAld's cross section is interpolated on P/100 (hPa). Upstream default 101325 Pa."
        },
        "H2O": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "ppb",
          "default": 450.0,
          "description": "Water-vapour mixing ratio (ppb); enters adjust_j_o31D only. Upstream default 450 ppb (the reference couples it from GEOS-FP RH)."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": 40.0,
          "description": "Latitude (degrees north). Upstream default 40."
        },
        "long": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg",
          "default": -97.0,
          "description": "Longitude (degrees east). Upstream default -97. Named `long` as upstream."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 1462060800.0,
          "description": "Reference Unix time (s) of t = 0; the absolute time is t + t_ref. Upstream takes it as the constructor argument (DomainInfo's t_ref); default 2016-05-01T00:00:00Z."
        },
        "t_utc": {"type": "unknown", "units": "s", "description": "Absolute UTC time (Unix s) = t + t_ref."},
        "DOY": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "UTC day of year (1 = Jan 1)."},
        "utc_hours": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "UTC hour of day, hour + minute/60 + second/3600 (upstream `hours`)."
        },
        "year": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "UTC calendar year."},
        "yearday_temp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "2*pi*(DOY - 1 + (hours - 12)/24), the un-normalised fractional-year angle."
        },
        "gamma": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Fractional-year angle (rad): yearday_temp/366 when mod(year, 4) == 0, else /365 (upstream's leap rule)."
        },
        "Eot": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "Equation of time (minutes)."},
        "timezone": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "floor(long/15): the nominal time-zone offset (hours)."
        },
        "time_offset": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "Eot + 4*(long - 15*timezone) (minutes)."},
        "t_local": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s",
          "description": "Zone-local time (Unix s) = t_utc + timezone*3600."
        },
        "tst": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1", "description": "True solar time (hours)."},
        "AHR": {"type": "unknown", "units": "rad", "description": "Hour angle (rad) = deg2rad(15)*(tst - 12)."},
        "LAT": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "description": "abs(lat) in radians. Upstream takes the absolute value (see notes: southern-hemisphere seasons are not flipped)."
        },
        "DEC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "description": "Solar declination (rad): asin(sin(deg2rad(-23.44)) * cos(deg2rad(360/365.24*(DOY+10) + 360/pi*0.0167*sin(deg2rad(360/365.24*(DOY-2))))))."
        },
        "cosSZA": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Cosine of the solar zenith angle (upstream cos_solar_zenith_angle; unclamped)."
        },
        "solf": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Earth-Sun distance factor on the TOA flux, 1 - 0.034*cos((DOY - 172)*2*pi/365) (upstream solar_flux_factor, after GEOS-Chem SOLAR_JX SOLFX)."
        },
        "F_187": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "Actinic flux in band 1 (187 nm): bilinear (P, cosSZA) lookup of upstream's total-flux table (direct + diffuse, tropospheric_interpolation_data.bson; flat outside the 1000-100000 Pa x -0.2..1.0 grid) times solf."
        },
