          "id": "diurnal_cycle",
          "description": "Photolysis rates through 1 May 2016 at 40N, 97W, at the surface, one point per UTC hour (t_ref = 2016-05-01T00Z + h hours): upstream's solar geometry sets cosSZA from t + t_ref, so the rates peak near 18Z (local solar noon) and fall to the twilight diffuse floor, then zero, at night.",
